    <span style="color:LightCoral">Then you see a pair of headlights turning down the street.</span> <br>
    <br>
    You panic, stumbling a little as your heart skips a beat. You only have a second to think, to figure out what to do. <span style="color:Yellow">Keep running to cover? You’ll be seen for sure! Try to hide? But where!? This stretch of sidewalk is so open, so exposed, the only place you could possibly hide would be… the car!</span> <br>
    <br>
    You turn on your heels, nearly losing your balance and falling straight into the small metal trashcan in front of the last house, which would sadly be too small to offer any real coverage, and dive for their large red SUV parked in the driveway. <span style="color:Yellow">You land hard on the cement but push past the pain as you roll under the car. While you could easily be spotted if someone was looking in your direction, this is the only cover you could find! So, you lie there, absolutely still and holding your breath as you wait for the car to pass by… <br>
    <br>
    15 seconds… 30 seconds… a minute…?</span> <br>
    <br>
    Where is it!? You swear it was turning down the street! Did it stop at a house!? No, this is the last one at the corner, you would see it! You swear it was turning down this street but… maybe it was going straight? <span style="color:LightCoral">You curse yourself quietly, your bruised knees more apparent as you realize the dive was all for nothing. You are about to crawl out from under the car when you hear something that makes your heart drop.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“H- hello?”</span> An old, shakily voice calls out as you hear a nearby door open. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Is someone there?”</span> The voice sounds like a grandma, and you peek out just enough to see a pair of slippered feet by the house’s front door. <span style="color:LightCoral">Damn it! She must have heard you when you dove for the car. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Could have sworn I heard something.”</span> You see a flashlight flicker on as the old woman shuffles down the patio stairs towards the driveway, shining her light across the lawn searching for the source of the noise.</span> <br>

